rguments and sometimes also to accept reasons on the opposite side."},{"id":"d7a37806-5acd-41bd-ab1a-695cd9c72073","text":"There is a better way to win arguments."},{"id":"c7e17ff2-4a50-4737-a596-2a644b84afd5","text":"Imagine that you favor increasing the minimum wage in our state, and I do not."},{"id":"1911a1b5-21bb-4733-a5a9-20b51e3b168e","text":"If you yell, “Yes,” and I yell, “No,” neither of us learns anything."},{"id":"fb079fcf-4fc9-41c0-a437-83d31d6790c7","text":"We neither understand nor respect each other, and we have no basis for compromise or cooperation."},{"id":"13c86c90-4a20-4770-a132-5acc3942e0cc","text":"In contrast, suppose you give a reasonable argument: that full-time workers should not have to live in poverty."},{"id":"dab3b844-7c68-4533-a462-8d0ce48909db","text":"Then I counter with another reasonable argument: that a higher minimum wage will force businesses to employ fewer people for less time."},{"id":"958053a7-8b3b-4da8-a595-98ed715cd00b","text":"Now we can understand each other’s positions and recognize our shared values, since we both care about needy workers."},{"id":"f12015db-b50b-461a-a370-df8a8b645782","text":"These views of arguments also undermine reason."},{"id":"82a4afda-c385-453d-a64f-f0532376cbf0","text":"If you see a conversation as a fight or competition, you can win by cheating as long as you don’t get caught."},{"id":"7e990ad6-90be-4031-adc2-d443f62e1b58","text":"You will be happy to convince people with bad arguments."},{"id":"6b795044-c6b3-4aa7-a7f7-8fa50fd31ac1","text":"You can call their views stupid, or joke about how ignorant they are."},{"id":"f36bd4be-fd13-4472-af27-3e13b44bf679","text":"None of these tricks will help you understand them, their positions or the issues that divide you, but they can help you win – in one way."},{"id":"5a7f69ba-8dac-4bca-a099-7a53f6685372","text":"In his 1936 work How to Win Friends and Influence People, Dale Carnegie wrote: “There is only one way…to get the best of an argument – and th