ble to use at least 15 journals as citation providers to articles published by five scientists at three universities."},{"id":"9f2bd94f-472a-49aa-a6c0-75ba9410f628","text":"The problem is rampant in Scopus, a citation database, which includes a high number of the new “international” journals."},{"id":"8411d2b9-d340-46e8-ae56-e383450d3789","text":"In fact, a listing in Scopus seems to be a criterion to be targeted in this type of citation manipulation."}]},{"id":"7694f145-bde3-4c74-aca7-7600272892ad","sentences":[{"id":"9ca4c440-2743-4404-a8b4-1a2a9ec70045","text":"Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice."},{"id":"d0b49354-c20e-426c-a47d-7774783f1ac5","text":"Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year."},{"id":"9ffdddcb-166f-43b3-a1da-ed4d4d2e7c2f","text":"And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal."}]}],"sentences":[{"id":"31a53d71-8bb8-4ef4-a5a2-10b3bc8f9d73","text":"Scientific papers are the recordkeepers of progress in research."},{"id":"9b392b30-0d3a-49de-afaf-2115ae66eda2","text":"Each year researchers publish millions of papers in more than 30,000 journals."},{"id":"0ff09b93-2a50-4d53-ad2c-e57bc4976fd2","text":"The scientific community measures the quality of those papers in a number of ways, including the perceived quality of the journal (as reflected by the title’s impact factor) and the number of citations a specific paper accumulates."},{"id":"1e27d330-f831-483e-a508-ac6e4027b9ab","text":"The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers."},{"id":"35b00a97-c47a-4b1f-a6e8-240e92709c7f","text":"Citation cartels, where journals, authors, and institutions conspire to inflate citation num