shed by five scientists at three universities."},{"id":"9f2bd94f-472a-49aa-a6c0-75ba9410f628","text":"The problem is rampant in Scopus, a citation database, which includes a high number of the new “international” journals."},{"id":"8411d2b9-d340-46e8-ae56-e383450d3789","text":"In fact, a listing in Scopus seems to be a criterion to be targeted in this type of citation manipulation."},{"id":"9ca4c440-2743-4404-a8b4-1a2a9ec70045","text":"Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice."},{"id":"d0b49354-c20e-426c-a47d-7774783f1ac5","text":"Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year."},{"id":"9ffdddcb-166f-43b3-a1da-ed4d4d2e7c2f","text":"And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
