3f-aff5-d71dba16a121","text":"They serve no purpose in a museum in the United States or elsewhere except as curious objects."},{"id":"77382ff3-5855-4fa2-af2d-722bf97cf969","text":"They cannot be compared to works of art produced for sale which can be passed from hand to hand and place to place by purchase."},{"id":"76e34ef8-8bbf-4c53-aab7-acd86e714c0f","text":"Buck"},{"id":"7f26ea7a-8c6b-4163-a87f-216d0daff07f","text":"We know very exact reproductions of artwork can be and are regularly produced."},{"id":"3c53f9b1-2328-43eb-a5de-1117ac99383c","text":"Perhaps museums and governments might explore some role for the use of nearly exact reproductions as a means of resolving issues relating to returning works of art and antiquities."},{"id":"d84ec63e-b8c9-407f-a332-b8db778744cc","text":"The context of any exhibit is more important to me than whether the object being displayed is 2000 years old or 2 months old."},{"id":"fd5c99d4-0e41-437a-ada7-26eb33c08788","text":"In many cases the experts have a hard time agreeing on what is the real object and what is a forgery."},{"id":"8f109b15-4a37-4594-aee9-64de9fdbb878","text":"Again, the story an exhibit is trying to tell is what matters."},{"id":"e8dcfac3-44d3-4bf7-a181-e4f1076cd3fe","text":"The monetary value of the objects on display is a distant second place in importance."},{"id":"32e2f40c-8862-4cc9-a00c-2e2b80e9cad1","text":"Sara"},{"id":"631be774-7f78-479f-a41a-a5a9edeca90e","text":"When visiting the Baltimore Museum of Art, I came across a magnificent 15th-century Chinese sculpture."},{"id":"d2f9b115-4de4-45e5-a5ff-957e4221961b","text":"It inspired me to learn more about the culture that it represented."},{"id":"e4ee880d-5127-4e5c-a9ae-d8b8be2c714a","text":"Artifacts in museums have the power to inspire, and perhaps spark that need to learn and understand the nature of their creators."},{"id":"b6b31099-2c76-4c38-a522-4da0b5c3c1f1","text":"Having said that, I do feel that whatever artifacts find their way to public museums should, in fact, be sanctioned as having been obtained on loan, legally purchased, or obtained by treaty."},{"id":"21b52b7d-8cb6-4a28-a532-5eeba11d5eca","text":"Stealing artifacts from other peoples’ cultures is obscene; it robs not only the physical objects, but the dignity and spirit of their creators."},{"id":"bf390250-88fa-48db-a5c2-503ec802b82e","text":"Victor"},{"id":"cafb2ca8-bbdb-4f3e-a3a3-59d0313cb169","text":"Ancient art that is displayed in foreign countries by all means should be returned to the original country."},{"id":"97f65166-00c8-47fe-a436-826eae655dd3","text":"The foreign countries have no right to hold back returning the items."},{"id":"e34c0680-0914-41b9-a189-9680c455d2ef","text":"I would ask that the foreign nations and the original country discuss the terms of transfer."},{"id":"1d59694c-6af4-4037-a850-c6fdead4cd4e","text":"Yes, there is the risk that the original country will not have as good security as do the foreign countries."},{"id":"5aab963c-053b-4d4f-a990-92c74d496a68","text":"But look at what happened to Boston’s Gardner Museum theft in 1990, including the loss of Rembrandt, Vermeer, Manet, and other masterpieces."},{"id":"3265f277-8df3-4647-ad53-08886eb138ac","text":"Nothing is absolutely safe, nowhere."},{"id":"5447eadc-696e-4b49-a7a1-6c235c0cd4ce","text":"And now Climate Change agitators are attacking publicly displayed works in European museums."},{"id":"20bc8c1d-61d6-47eb-a41f-20da6e786c86","text":"Julia"},{"id":"237b3151-a920-42b9-a484-af9f25c6452a","text":"To those of you in the comments section who are having strong feelings about artifacts being removed from cities in the US and Britain and returned to their countries of origin, I would ask you to consider: why do you think Americans have more of a right to easily access the Benin Bronzes than the people of Nigeria?"},{"id":"4f7834de-8899-43ea-ac00-7f289fd1a126","text":"Why are people who live within a day’s drive of London entitled to go and see the Elgin Marbles whenever they want, but the people of Athens aren’t?"},{"id":"7eecbae5-c322-4b7e-adf7-465177fd79fe","text":"What intrinsic factors make the West a suitable home for these artifacts but preclude them from being preserved and displayed by their countries of origin?"},{"id":"c6948961-2968-4d68-adc1-9c363d339a3f","text":"If your conclusion is that the West is better able to preserve these artifacts, think about why you’re assuming that to be true."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
