productions to Los Angeles. Let’s go on with the show... and make sure the show doesn’t go on without us.","paragraphs":[{"id":"931449c8-a0b8-4279-a9db-a7c973867056","sentences":[{"id":"5cbadbf7-478a-468b-aa51-2f2e0095247a","text":"There''s no business like show business—but in Los Angeles, it feels like there''s no business at all."},{"id":"ed9c1a99-1319-4658-abb3-1f79b4760ef1","text":"If that sounds melodramatic, consider this: The Art Directors Guild, a labor union representing about 3,000 film workers, has suspended a training program and issued a statement explaining that “we cannot in good conscience encourage you to pursue our profession.”"},{"id":"a3911da1-277b-4187-aa93-3769bc7f7456","text":"The guild’s pessimism is a reaction to Hollywood’s decline, which is reaching a critical point for the industry and Southern California."}]},{"id":"649197bf-91b3-4d55-a4ae-5669a42cc7e5","sentences":[{"id":"ea8589e6-19cb-4765-a57b-c603a253f0a5","text":"Production has been slipping away from Hollywood since the 1950s, but the effects have never been more apparent than at present."},{"id":"3704f068-cc17-4311-a3df-092e77bdc5ad","text":"Other regions in the United States, Canada and Europe have steadily increased incentives to attract TV shows and movies, leaving California in the dust."},{"id":"4093d552-f810-4d28-acb9-5c75540ceb21","text":"Georgia offers up to 30% in transferable tax credits on film and TV production costs, plus an additional 10% increase on the base tax credit if the project includes a Georgia promotional logo."}]},{"id":"528ab3eb-0f0f-49f2-ab70-ad168424e3c9","sentences":[{"id":"7a2ecb94-c191-479e-a8b0-233a17aa8430","text":"Even as California lost a huge volume of production to other locations, there was still plenty of film production taking place in Los Angeles before this year."},{"id":"1d838313-5fdd-41b6-a6c8-6f783ab0ea3c","text":"We were kept afloat by “peak TV”, the glut of content that was required by the explosion of streaming services."}]},{"id":"099e370c-f582-45e5-af9a-7b2ba350c45b","sentences":[{"id":"b39b4244-0188-4a11-a259-fcee55d6b10c","text":"If productions in Southern California dip below a critical level for too long, the industry’s essential talent will drift away along with enormous sums of revenue."},{"id":"2adafcb4-14e7-4a00-a729-ce8120c7b310","text":"Persuading studios to film here would become much more challenging if we couldn’t offer a deep bench of local film workers, on-screen talent and local businesses that support the entertainment industry."}]},{"id":"b51b1166-7407-4fcb-a6f6-1b1ce2abff41","sentences":[{"id":"e106bbf4-6a21-4d2d-ae72-774560aeed1b","text":"That''s why the California Film Commission and its Los Angeles counterpart, FilmLA, should act now, before it''s too late."},{"id":"f5a39cdf-4e89-4a5a-a5fd-9203a341996d","text":"Those agencies and other government bodies should dramatically improve incentives to keep our current shows and attract new productions to Los Angeles."},{"id":"d8495264-3587-489a-ac79-4abd9a7357fe","text":"Let’s go on with the show... and make sure the show doesn’t go on without us."}]}],"sentences":[{"id":"5cbadbf7-478a-468b-aa51-2f2e0095247a","text":"There''s no business like show business—but in Los Angeles, it feels like there''s no business at all."},{"id":"ed9c1a99-1319-4658-abb3-1f79b4760ef1","text":"If that sounds melodramatic, consider this: The Art Directors Guild, a labor union representing about 3,000 film workers, has suspended a training program and issued a statement explaining that “we cannot in good conscience encourage you to pursue our profession.”"},{"id":"a3911da1-277b-4187-aa93-3769bc7f7456","text":"The guild’s pessimism is a reaction to Hollywood’s decline, which is reaching a critical point for the industry and Southern California."},{"id":"ea8589e6-19cb-4765-a57b-c603a253f0a5","text":"Production has been slipping away from Hollywood since the 1950s, but the effects have never been more apparent than at present."},{"id":"3704f068-cc17-4311-a3df-092e77bdc5ad","text":"Other regions in the United States, Canada and Europe have steadily increased incentives to attract TV shows and movies, leaving California in the dust."},{"id":"4093d552-f810-4d28-acb9-5c75540ceb21","text":"Georgia offers up to 30% in transferable tax credits on film and TV production costs, plus an additional 10% increase on the base tax credit if the project includes a Georgia promotional logo."},{"id":"7a2ecb94-c191-479e-a8b0-233a17aa8430","text":"Even as California lost a huge volume of production to other locations, there was still plenty of film production taking place in Los Angeles before this year."},{"id":"1d838313-5fdd-41b6-a6c8-6f783ab0ea3c","text":"We were kept afloat by “peak TV”, the glut of content that was required by the explosion of streaming services."},{"id":"b39b4244-0188-4a11-a259-fcee55d6b10c","text":"If productions in Southern California dip below a critical level for too long, the industry’s essential talent will drift away along with enormous sums of revenue."},{"id":"2adafcb4-14e7-4a00-a729-ce8120c7b310","text":"Persuading studios to film here would become much more challenging if we couldn’t offer a deep bench of local film workers, on-screen talent and local businesses that support the entertainment industry."},{"id":"e106bbf4-6a21-4d2d-ae72-774560aeed1b","text":"That''s why the California Film Commission and its Los Angeles counterpart, FilmLA, should act now, before it''s too late."},{"id":"f5a39cdf-4e89-4a5a-a5fd-9203a341996d","text":"Those agencies and other government bodies should dramatically improve incentives to keep our current shows and attract new productions to Los Angeles."},{"id":"d8495264-3587-489a-ac79-4abd9a7357fe","text":"Let’s go on with the show... and make sure the show doesn’t go on without us."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
