 that frequent, low-severity fires made many ecosystems healthier."},{"id":"dc0b8b07-5786-46a9-ace1-d72d9e37f794","text":"They rid the forest of dead and sick trees, reducing competition and curbing the spread of disease."},{"id":"cc1a188d-f003-4e8c-a91e-0d5ccf191acf","text":"Because flammable material couldn’t build up on the landscape, blazes tended to move slowly and peter out when they reached the footprints of previous burns."}]},{"id":"ac3e39b8-5c61-4d1e-a2f3-50b76094d19d","sentences":[{"id":"fa7e3c22-5039-427c-a22c-5372c0f2dd53","text":"In 2022, Swetnam and other scientists teamed up to compile a database of fire-scarred trees from across the continent."},{"id":"acab2489-3eb8-4989-a1fe-b5d74fad17df","text":"Their North American tree-ring fire-scar network (NAFSN) provided the basis for a study published last month."},{"id":"6d49f971-6a04-485b-a3cf-e694d837bdd9","text":"In the study, the researchers compared the historical fire cadence with the wildfires recorded over the past few decades, and uncovered a striking shortfall."},{"id":"efa4aeb1-450e-4fcc-a1cc-54f8fc07ab2f","text":"The NAFSN sites experienced less than a quarter of the number of fires that would have been expected without fire suppression."}]},{"id":"3737a4fe-6f99-4a9d-a8cd-ccd1208b6a49","sentences":[{"id":"130b8386-49c8-4bc8-a412-3509f61d3ca3","text":"This deficit is a testament to the effectiveness of modern firefighting, said Kelly Martin, a past president of the International Association of Wildland Fire."},{"id":"75c538ac-0d2c-4a8d-ad6f-cd542bee0b8e","text":"“Yet the combined consequences of suppression and climate change have eroded humanity’s ability to suppress fires, particularly those that ignite under the most dangerous weather conditions.”"}]},{"id":"95c70482-c308-4ddf-aaa7-ce2c6e126f40","sentences":[{"id":"99029707-62a3-40f0-a9d7-27f1f2bcd064","text":"To prevent entire ecosystems from going up in smoke, Martin said, people must bring healthy fire back to places that need it."},{"id":"74cdd8fe-74e6-4d5e-a236-d793d4ce9321","text":"At Yosemite National Park, Martin oversaw the use of what is known as prescribed burns to make the landscape more resilient."},{"id":"57a6fa53-623b-4264-a4ac-2d8e97642e95","text":"These fires were carefully planned and intentionally ignited during periods when weather kept the blazes easy to control, and helped eliminate some of the fuel that had built up around the important park’s facilities."},{"id":"e84e8539-0723-40d4-a054-5845715a570e","text":"Research shows that these prescribed burns make subsequent wildfires less severe, even if later fires happen under the most dangerous weather conditions."}]},{"id":"357a6cd0-d2f3-4a27-ab9c-c78700e59b6f","sentences":[{"id":"21870120-aefd-4437-a997-96b34ca4b98a","text":"Yet even as scientists and public officials increasingly agree on the need for more fires in our forests, climate change is making this tactic more challenging, experts said."},{"id":"86f194f5-5df6-4604-a86c-2853dd64e2c1","text":"“It’s a double-edged sword because wildfires are getting more severe and larger under climate change and we need this work even more, but then the work gets more challenging,” said Susan Prichard, a fire ecologist at the University of Washington."}]}],"sentences":[{"id":"f4fb5478-ced1-4ccd-a8a2-06b933c3c234","text":"When Tom Swetnam joined the U.S."},{"id":"a809945d-4c6f-4eeb-a9cb-89daf7925f4f","text":"Forest Service in the 1970s, his mandate was to “put everything out,” he recalled."},{"id":"bec4d2ed-9498-41f9-a3bc-139f83365cae","text":"But when Swetnam enrolled in graduate school at the University of Arizona’s Laboratory of Tree-Ring Research, he was surprised to find a record of repeated blazes dating back hundreds of years before European colonists arrived on the continent."},{"id":"2a981de4-a821-4e30-a50a-90bfebea846b","text":"Some of the trees he analyzed bore more than 20 fire scars among their rings."},{"id":"ac1635f6-9094-4448-af85-91ce3c452423","text":"The fact that fires happened so often meant they couldn’t have been severe enough to kill most trees."},{"id":"4fe02b93-d156-4ab1-a9da-37efa863aa00","text":"Instead, a growing body of research showed that frequent, low-severity fires made many ecosystems healthier."},{"id":"dc0b8b07-5786-46a9-ace1-d72d9e37f794","text":"They rid the forest of dead and sick trees, reducing competition and curbing the spread of disease."},{"id":"cc1a188d-f003-4e8c-a91e-0d5ccf191acf","text":"Because flammable material couldn’t build up on the landscape, blazes tended to move slowly and peter out when they reached the footprints of previous burns."},{"id":"fa7e3c22-5039-427c-a22c-5372c0f2dd53","text":"In 2022, Swetnam and other scientists teamed up to compile a database of fire-scarred trees from across the continent."},{"id":"acab2489-3eb8-4989-a1fe-b5d74fad17df","text":"Their North American tree-ring fire-scar network (NAFSN) provided the basis for a study published last month."},{"id":"6d49f971-6a04-485b-a3cf-e694d837bdd9","text":"In the study, the researchers compared the historical fire cadence with the wildfires recorded over the past few decades, and uncovered a striking shortfall."},{"id":"efa4aeb1-450e-4fcc-a1cc-54f8fc07ab2f","text":"The NAFSN sites experienced less than a quarter of the number of fires that would have been expected without fire suppression."},{"id":"130b8386-49c8-4bc8-a412-3509f61d3ca3","text":"This deficit is a testament to the effectiveness of modern firefighting, said Kelly Martin, a past president of the International Association of Wildland Fire."},{"id":"75c538ac-0d2c-4a8d-ad6f-cd542bee0b8e","text":"“Yet the combined consequences of suppression and climate change have eroded humanity’s ability to suppress fires, particularly those that ignite under the most dangerous weather conditions.”"},{"id":"99029707-62a3-40f0-a9d7-27f1f2bcd064","text":"To prevent entire ecosystems from going up in smoke, Martin said, people must bring healthy fire back to places that need it."},{"id":"74cdd8fe-74e6-4d5e-a236-d793d4ce9321","text":"At Yosemite National Park, Martin oversaw the use of what is known as prescribed burns to make the landscape more resilient."},{"id":"57a6fa53-623b-4264-a4ac-2d8e97642e95","text":"These fires were carefully planned and intentionally ignited during periods when weather kept the blazes easy to control, and helped eliminate some of the fuel that had built up around the important park’s facilities."},{"id":"e84e8539-0723-40d4-a054-5845715a570e","text":"Research shows that these prescribed burns make subsequent wildfires less severe, even if later fires happen under the most dangerous weather conditions."},{"id":"21870120-aefd-4437-a997-96b34ca4b98a","text":"Yet even as scientists and public officials increasingly agree on the need for more fires in our forests, climate change is making this tactic more challenging, experts said."},{"id":"86f194f5-5df6-4604-a86c-2853dd64e2c1","text":"“It’s a double-edged sword because wildfires are getting more severe and larger under climate change and we need this work even more, but then the work gets more challenging,” said Susan Prichard, a fire ecologist at the University of Washington."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
