 or Olga Tokarczuk), classic (Virginia Woolf or James Baldwin) or genre (Stephen King, Margaret Atwood, Georges Simenon) – it doesn’t matter."},{"id":"724f5da3-cfaa-4a40-a284-f6c23ee32ce1","text":"Fiction invites you to loiter the unseen."},{"id":"58318b57-1ff8-4797-a3a5-63c0cf6e6ed6","text":"In the lives of others."},{"id":"54f8bad6-0875-4089-a66c-7666fac95607","text":"We are living through a golden age of translation too, so you can go anywhere in time or place."},{"id":"c565c377-3a89-4c72-aaee-665a4b489aff","text":"And just read a single poem."},{"id":"52befdb0-9827-4f46-aed7-24d2eb2621c0","text":"In his Oxford lectures, Seamus Heaney argued that a poem draws a picture of reality, a “glimpsed alternative” that sets up a contradiction with your own, in ways little and large."},{"id":"2980525f-1ca5-4153-a2d0-e90a3ac426e6","text":"The negotiation, between you and it, is the heart of the matter."},{"id":"622badf0-aa71-4ac8-aa8f-8f5f403947fd","text":"What does the poet see that you don’t?"},{"id":"7320cac2-0ea3-4d9f-a46c-23cfc365782d","text":"What does the difference mean?"},{"id":"6eacd492-b4a3-4984-a53f-59145dd3fc17","text":"It could be one of the best conversations you ever have."},{"id":"9a4bfd81-295a-4e1b-ae94-8def181b5d38","text":"Forget self-help books; reading is self-help in action."},{"id":"aa91efae-8dde-4bd9-a871-70d6153223bd","text":"Neuroscientists have been at pains to demonstrate that the pleasure a book provides isn’t indulgence; it’s good for you."},{"id":"09e07125-aba5-4d7b-adeb-4636ec00b838","text":"Reading will keep you better informed about the world but it can also improve our tech-shattered ability to concentrate."},{"id":"b27a9b85-859c-4052-adf4-4d16ca529eca","text":"Standing in the shoes of others fine tunes our social understanding, useful as we struggle to understand friends, neighbours, customers and co-workers."},{"id":"9f10b6b8-fe12-457b-ada3-821683e66ea5","text":"Different parts of our brain engage as we simulate scenes, characters and mental states."},{"id":"d714c432-947d-4f86-a2a2-ecb8e2c80fff","text":"Our imagination – remember that? – is rekindled."},{"id":"5f6264e5-7806-42cc-a351-be82bb2abc08","text":"Reading has also been found to make us more helpful, to reduce bias, and even to increase longevity – something we will enjoy all the more if we have a good book in our hands."},{"id":"64ee7910-e469-4bdc-a6a8-d6d4d9021793","text":"(And yes, all these benefits are more closely associated with physical books than digital ones.)"},{"id":"f3e8f1ff-9ffc-4e66-adbd-6e9eb5ecce4b","text":"It is undoubtedly true that all work and no play really does make Jack, or Jill, dull."},{"id":"464d44a1-ab32-48ff-a003-fe9ed034e0a9","text":"The cure is right at hand, reading is cheap, easy and, most important, it’s fun."},{"id":"a35f282e-f024-4e91-acd0-eba60fb6aa41","text":"Liberate your imagination this year."}],"currentSentenceIndex":0,"origin":"system"}'::jsonb,
